And they're like, "All
right, give us 10 names,"

00:23:15.627 --> 00:23:16.661 align:start size:84% position:16%
and you give me up
and I don't blame you.

00:23:16.661 --> 00:23:18.130
You're like, "All right, Malice.

00:23:18.130 --> 00:23:20.399 align:start position:0%
It's Shapiro, it's Jordan
Peterson, it's Governor Sanders.

00:23:20.399 --> 00:23:21.600 align:start size:84% position:16%
Yeah, we're all
conspiring together.

00:23:21.600 --> 00:23:22.801
Just leave my kids alone,"

00:23:22.801 --> 00:23:24.302
right?
- Right.

00:23:24.302 --> 00:23:27.606
- What actually happened is
the Stasi recruiters said

00:23:27.606 --> 00:23:29.241 align:start size:84% position:16%
a lot of these people
were just bored.

00:23:29.241 --> 00:23:30.742 align:start size:84% position:16%
We didn't have to
put pressure on them.

00:23:30.742 --> 00:23:33.478 align:start size:97% position:3%
They came to us because they
wanted to feel important.

00:23:33.478 --> 00:23:35.714
They wanted to feel like they
were doing the right thing.

00:23:35.714 --> 00:23:37.716
They wanted someone to just
actually listen to them.

00:23:37.716 --> 00:23:39.351
We barely paid them anything.

00:23:39.351 --> 00:23:41.319
And when you hear this,

00:23:41.319 --> 00:23:44.122
speaking to me like having a
naive view of human nature,

00:23:44.122 --> 00:23:45.924
people in America
need to appreciate,

00:23:45.924 --> 00:23:48.093
and I think COVID opened
a lot of people's eyes.

00:23:48.093 --> 00:23:49.327
- [Dave] Yeah.

00:23:49.327 --> 00:23:51.329
- How eager the
average person is

00:23:51.329 --> 00:23:53.098
to be an informant
on their neighbors.

00:23:53.098 --> 00:23:54.933
It's not like you
think in the movies

00:23:54.933 --> 00:23:57.936
where Tom Cruise has a gun to
his head and he is like, ah.

00:23:57.936 --> 00:24:00.272 align:start size:84% position:16%
And he is like, 'Fine,
I'll name names."

00:24:00.272 --> 00:24:01.807
No, it's like they
knock on your door,

00:24:01.807 --> 00:24:05.110
and they're like, "Hey, I saw
Dave and Malice having a talk.

00:24:05.110 --> 00:24:06.044
Maybe they're up to something.

00:24:06.044 --> 00:24:07.112
You should go check them out."

00:24:07.112 --> 00:24:08.713
And now he feels
like a big shot.

00:24:08.713 --> 00:24:10.348
- Yeah that's a ...

00:24:10.348 --> 00:24:12.150
Did you never think, I mean,

00:24:12.150 --> 00:24:14.586 align:start size:88% position:13%
'cause you are obviously
fairly well-read

00:24:14.586 --> 00:24:16.021
and have been around the world.

00:24:16.021 --> 00:24:17.422
When COVID was happening

00:24:17.422 --> 00:24:19.724
and we were hunting
down people at stores

00:24:19.724 --> 00:24:20.959
for not wearing masks,

00:24:20.959 --> 00:24:22.427
which I always thought
it was the funniest.

00:24:22.427 --> 00:24:24.062
The crazy woman in the
mask hunting down the guy

00:24:24.062 --> 00:24:25.297
for not wearing a mask.

00:24:25.297 --> 00:24:26.498
You'd think you'd be
running the other way,

00:24:26.498 --> 00:24:28.567
but they were always
running to tackle them.

00:24:28.567 --> 00:24:29.501
Did you?

00:24:29.501 --> 00:24:30.735
- It's like a zombie movie.

00:24:30.735 --> 00:24:32.304
It's like I better go
fight those zombies.

00:24:32.304 --> 00:24:33.872
No, go away from the zombies.

00:24:33.872 --> 00:24:35.407 align:start position:0%
- Right, it was a reverse zombie
movie, something like that.

00:24:35.407 --> 00:24:37.242
It was like zombie Bizarro land.

00:24:37.242 --> 00:24:38.710
But that sort of thing.

00:24:38.710 --> 00:24:41.580 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, when it was unfolding
and you were in Brooklyn,

00:24:41.580 --> 00:24:43.615
which, so you're
on top of people

00:24:43.615 --> 00:24:44.816
quite literally, right?

00:24:44.816 --> 00:24:46.284 align:start size:84% position:16%
You literally have
people right above you

00:24:46.284 --> 00:24:47.819
and right below you.

00:24:47.819 --> 00:24:50.989
Did you think that it was
gonna unravel so quickly?

00:24:50.989 --> 00:24:52.924
- I was very surprised.

00:24:52.924 --> 00:24:54.459
I was very surprised.

00:24:54.459 --> 00:24:56.461
I had this tweet, which I
got a lot of pushback for,

00:24:56.461 --> 00:24:59.231
and I stand by very much
where I said, if you ...

00:24:59.231 --> 00:25:01.433
'cause one of the big questions

00:25:01.433 --> 00:25:04.302
that humanity always asked is
how did Hitler come to power,

00:25:04.302 --> 00:25:06.505 align:start size:97% position:3%
and how did those atrocities
were allowed to happen?

00:25:06.505 --> 00:25:09.107
'Cause we gotta make sure
whatever those steps were

00:25:09.107 --> 00:25:10.775 align:start size:84% position:16%
aren't replicated
in any other country

00:25:10.775 --> 00:25:12.143
or any other population.

00:25:12.143 --> 00:25:13.612
And this was always like,

00:25:13.612 --> 00:25:14.980 align:start size:97% position:3%
was there something uniquely
about the German people?

00:25:14.980 --> 00:25:15.914
It something uniquely about him?

00:25:15.914 --> 00:25:17.148
Was it the economic conditions?

00:25:17.148 --> 00:25:18.683
Was it with the
Weimar situation?

00:25:18.683 --> 00:25:22.287 align:start size:84% position:16%
And what I think
people just learned,

00:25:22.287 --> 00:25:24.089
I tweeted out, I said,

00:25:24.089 --> 00:25:27.259
"If you replaced the word
Jews with coronavirus,

00:25:27.259 --> 00:25:30.061
suddenly the behavior of
the 1930s German population

00:25:30.061 --> 00:25:31.363 align:start size:88% position:13%
becomes a lot clearer."
- Yeah.

00:25:31.363 --> 00:25:32.697
- Oh, how can you say this?

00:25:32.697 --> 00:25:34.132
- I remember this one, yeah.

00:25:34.132 --> 00:25:38.937 align:start position:0%
- The point is, we saw no
matter where you stand on COVID,

00:25:39.804 --> 00:25:40.906
where you stand on vaccination,

00:25:40.906 --> 00:25:44.576 align:start size:84% position:16%
you saw how
effectively the media,

00:25:44.576 --> 00:25:47.712
maybe even correctly
create an outgroup,

00:25:47.712 --> 00:25:51.449
the vitriol with which
people were attacked.

00:25:51.449 --> 00:25:54.753 align:start size:84% position:16%
The glee, I'm glad
they're getting fired.

00:25:54.753 --> 00:25:56.721 align:start size:97% position:3%
These people should be
driven from polite society.

00:25:56.721 --> 00:25:58.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
They shouldn't be allowed
to leave their homes,

00:25:58.590 --> 00:26:00.892 align:start size:97% position:3%
they shouldn't be allowed
to get jobs, blah blah blah.

00:26:00.892 --> 00:26:04.162 align:start size:84% position:16%
Even after it was
clear that vaccination

00:26:04.162 --> 00:26:05.864
is not gonna prevent
you from getting COVID,

00:26:05.864 --> 00:26:09.100
it's only gonna prevent the
severity of your illness.

00:26:09.100 --> 00:26:10.769
- And by the way, that's
even unclear at this point.

00:26:10.769 --> 00:26:12.337 align:start size:84% position:16%
- But I'm just trying
to steelmanning

00:26:12.337 --> 00:26:13.838 align:start size:97% position:3%
as much as possible, right?
- Okay.

00:26:13.838 --> 00:26:15.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
- So I'm trying to look
it from their perspective.

00:26:15.040 --> 00:26:18.109
Even given all that, the hatred,

00:26:18.109 --> 00:26:20.745 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the lack of
perception of those

00:26:20.745 --> 00:26:22.247
who are in opposition as human.

00:26:22.247 --> 00:26:23.915
And also the idea that like,

00:26:23.915 --> 00:26:25.517
you want me to die,

00:26:25.517 --> 00:26:27.819 align:start size:84% position:16%
so why should I care
about you at all?

00:26:27.819 --> 00:26:29.754
When you saw that mass drop,

00:26:29.754 --> 00:26:31.423
and you saw how
prevalent it was,

00:26:31.423 --> 00:26:33.992 align:start position:0%
I think that was very
revelatory for a lot of people.

00:26:33.992 --> 00:26:36.461
And it was surprising
to me as an American

00:26:36.461 --> 00:26:40.031 align:start size:97% position:3%
because I thought America
would have a lot more pushback

00:26:40.031 --> 00:26:41.700
than it had.

00:26:41.700 --> 00:26:43.535 align:start size:97% position:3%
But that's just kind of
information you have to choose

00:26:43.535 --> 00:26:45.003
and go forward with.

00:26:45.003 --> 00:26:48.006 align:start size:97% position:3%
- So as a guy that obviously
is not for a lot of laws

00:26:48.006 --> 00:26:49.541
to say the least.
- Correct, yes.

00:26:49.541 --> 00:26:50.809
(Michael laughs)

00:26:50.809 --> 00:26:53.144
- They come in with
mandates and shots,

00:26:53.144 --> 00:26:56.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they're firing people,
and all of this stuff.

00:26:56.715 --> 00:26:58.450 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then it all
turns out in essence,

00:26:58.450 --> 00:27:00.685
at least from my opinion, to
be completely unwarranted.

00:27:00.685 --> 00:27:03.021
I fortunately was against
all of it the entire time.

00:27:03.021 --> 00:27:04.823 align:start size:84% position:16%
I am not vaxed, they
will never inject

00:27:04.823 --> 00:27:07.325
this stuff in me,
blah, blah blah.

00:27:07.325 --> 00:27:08.860 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Can I interrupt?
- Yeah.

00:27:08.860 --> 00:27:10.061
- It's also different now
that you're a dad, right?

00:27:10.061 --> 00:27:11.529 align:start size:84% position:16%
Because now your
kids are threatened.

00:27:11.529 --> 00:27:12.964
It's a very different calculus.

00:27:12.964 --> 00:27:14.132 align:start size:84% position:16%
- So what do you think
about this theory?

00:27:14.132 --> 00:27:15.634 align:start size:88% position:13%
I've said this a couple
times on the show.

00:27:15.634 --> 00:27:17.669
I think that one of the
reasons they went so deep

00:27:17.669 --> 00:27:22.140
on vaxing the kids who
were at no risk, right?

00:27:22.140 --> 00:27:25.710
They were never at any risk,
was not because of the kids,

00:27:25.710 --> 00:27:27.245
it was because they figured,

00:27:27.245 --> 00:27:30.882
somehow they figured that if
you can get a parent to ...

00:27:30.882 --> 00:27:32.717
it's one thing to do
it to yourself, right?

00:27:32.717 --> 00:27:34.185
And then have to deal
with the repercussions

00:27:34.185 --> 00:27:36.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
if there's a vaccine
injury or something else.

00:27:36.321 --> 00:27:38.690 align:start size:97% position:3%
But once you can get a parent
to do it to their child,

00:27:38.690 --> 00:27:42.060
if you now find out the
child has enlarged heart

00:27:42.060 --> 00:27:45.463 align:start size:97% position:3%
or a series of other problems
that are now arising,

00:27:45.463 --> 00:27:47.399 align:start size:84% position:16%
your ability to deal
with that reality

00:27:47.399 --> 00:27:49.901
that you had something to
do with it is so shattering

00:27:49.901 --> 00:27:52.103 align:start position:0%
you can almost do anything
with that person at that point.

00:27:52.103 --> 00:27:53.304 align:start size:84% position:16%
Do you think there's
something there?

00:27:53.304 --> 00:27:55.407 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Absolutely, and
here's the other thing.

00:27:55.407 --> 00:27:57.175
From their perspective,

00:27:57.175 --> 00:27:59.177 align:start position:0%
I've never even heard a
counterargument to this really.

00:27:59.177 --> 00:28:00.845
And people can feel
free to yell at me

00:28:00.845 --> 00:28:02.380
all they want on social media.

00:28:02.380 --> 00:28:04.082 align:start size:84% position:16%
The argument is 'cause
we know the vaccine

00:28:04.082 --> 00:28:05.784
is limited efficacy, right?

00:28:05.784 --> 00:28:09.354
So you're saying this
kid who can't get COVID

00:28:09.354 --> 00:28:11.322
is going to get boosters every,

00:28:11.322 --> 00:28:14.325
an injection every six
months in perpetuity?

00:28:14.325 --> 00:28:16.161
Like that's what
you are positing.

00:28:16.161 --> 00:28:19.564 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I don't understand
even a bad reason for that.

00:28:19.564 --> 00:28:21.966
There still is, I'm not
COVID expert at all,

00:28:21.966 --> 00:28:23.835
but I still have not
seen any argument for,

00:28:23.835 --> 00:28:25.970 align:start size:84% position:16%
or against symptomless
transmission

00:28:25.970 --> 00:28:27.672
that seems to kind of
be swept under the rug.

00:28:27.672 --> 00:28:28.907
- Yep.

00:28:28.907 --> 00:28:33.244
- And I think it's
very, very sinister

00:28:33.244 --> 00:28:35.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you have kind of
going after people's kids.

00:28:35.980 --> 00:28:37.916
And also the other thing is,

00:28:37.916 --> 00:28:42.020 align:start size:97% position:3%
they have turned children
from the perception of parents

00:28:42.020 --> 00:28:43.788
as vectors of disease.

00:28:43.788 --> 00:28:47.192 align:start position:0%
So that's a mechanism to
separate the kid from the parent

00:28:47.192 --> 00:28:49.294
in some psychological sense.

00:28:49.294 --> 00:28:53.331 align:start size:88% position:13%
So I think all this
stuff is very sinister,

00:28:54.632 --> 00:28:56.701
and I want to hear if
I can ask a question.

00:28:56.701 --> 00:28:57.936
- [Dave] Yeah.

00:28:57.936 --> 00:29:00.171 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I thought that all
of these mandates

00:29:00.171 --> 00:29:02.540
and vaccine passports
were never going away.

00:29:02.540 --> 00:29:04.542
And the fact that
they receded at all

00:29:04.542 --> 00:29:07.112 align:start position:0%
in many of these cities is
something I was surprised about.

00:29:07.112 --> 00:29:07.946
Were you?

00:29:09.380 --> 00:29:12.217
- I'm not surprised that they
went away in the red states

00:29:12.217 --> 00:29:14.219
as really as DeSantis-

00:29:14.219 --> 00:29:15.453 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Well, no, but like
in New York City.

00:29:15.453 --> 00:29:16.688
- Yeah.

00:29:16.688 --> 00:29:17.622
- You don't have
to have a vaccine

00:29:17.622 --> 00:29:19.090
to go to a restaurant anymore.

00:29:19.090 --> 00:29:20.291
- So I'm not surprised
that once things started,

00:29:20.291 --> 00:29:21.826
once the narrative
shifted a little bit,

00:29:21.826 --> 00:29:23.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the red states really
did the right thing.

00:29:23.228 --> 00:29:24.395 align:start size:84% position:16%
'Cause they didn't all
do the right thing.

00:29:24.395 --> 00:29:25.663
People think the red states

00:29:25.663 --> 00:29:26.831
all did the right
thing immediately.

00:29:26.831 --> 00:29:28.099
It's not the case.

00:29:28.099 --> 00:29:29.534
And even DeSantis, by
the way, did lock down

00:29:29.534 --> 00:29:30.802
at the beginning,

00:29:30.802 --> 00:29:32.036
but then people want
to get him on this.

00:29:32.036 --> 00:29:33.838 align:start size:88% position:13%
But it's like then he
learned after two weeks,

00:29:33.838 --> 00:29:35.140
it was like, no, no more.

00:29:35.140 --> 00:29:36.975
So, okay, there's that.

00:29:36.975 --> 00:29:38.977
On the blue cities, I did think

00:29:38.977 --> 00:29:41.379 align:start size:97% position:3%
that it was gonna hold a
little bit longer than it did.

00:29:41.379 --> 00:29:43.248
So that at least has been nice.

00:29:43.248 --> 00:29:44.749
But it's left the cities,

00:29:44.749 --> 00:29:47.685
the rest of the residue of it
I think has left the cities

00:29:47.685 --> 00:29:48.887
with all sorts of problems.

00:29:48.887 --> 00:29:50.655
And all the good
people left, right?

00:29:50.655 --> 00:29:52.257
As you said, all your
friends, they left.

00:29:52.257 --> 00:29:53.658
So they were most
likely somewhat

00:29:53.658 --> 00:29:55.460
functional members of society.

00:29:55.460 --> 00:29:56.928
- But it's an intriguing-

00:29:56.928 --> 00:29:57.929
- And now they've brought
their skills to Austin

00:29:57.929 --> 00:29:59.097
and families and
everything else.

00:29:59.097 --> 00:30:00.565 align:start size:84% position:16%
- But it's an
intriguing question

00:30:00.565 --> 00:30:02.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I don't have an answer
as to why I was wrong,

00:30:02.167 --> 00:30:04.469
and why they did pull back.

00:30:04.469 --> 00:30:06.104
And also at the same time,

00:30:06.104 --> 00:30:09.407
it's still illegal for a
foreigner to visit America

00:30:09.407 --> 00:30:10.308
unless they're vaccinated.

00:30:10.308 --> 00:30:11.142
They just got extended-

00:30:11.142 --> 00:30:12.277
- They just extended it.

00:30:12.277 --> 00:30:16.114 align:start size:88% position:13%
- So there is a
incongruity here, and I-

00:30:16.114 --> 00:30:17.615
- Well, do you think
it's possibly that it's

00:30:17.615 --> 00:30:18.817
you can't do everything at once?

00:30:18.817 --> 00:30:20.151
So this was the first salvo.

00:30:20.151 --> 00:30:21.586
Let's see how far
we can push it.

00:30:21.586 --> 00:30:25.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were able to basically
grade the pushback

00:30:25.757 --> 00:30:26.958
and now we'll do it again.

00:30:26.958 --> 00:30:28.426
Sort of like in Canada,

00:30:28.426 --> 00:30:30.295 align:start size:97% position:3%
like you push back a certain
amount on the truckers,

00:30:30.295 --> 00:30:32.063
you see how much
pushback there is.

00:30:32.063 --> 00:30:33.164 align:start size:81% position:19%
And then of course
Trudeau's gonna

00:30:33.164 --> 00:30:34.632
do something else in a year.

00:30:34.632 --> 00:30:36.801
Like that you can't just ram
through everything in one shot.

00:30:36.801 --> 00:30:39.070
- But the thing is they
had rammed it through.

00:30:39.070 --> 00:30:41.005
So why didn't they normalize

00:30:41.005 --> 00:30:42.640
vaccine passports
in restaurants?

00:30:42.640 --> 00:30:44.609
'Cause that would be
a very effective tool.

00:30:44.609 --> 00:30:45.844
And especially they
had the app, right?

00:30:45.844 --> 00:30:47.245
So now you have an app to see

00:30:47.245 --> 00:30:49.414 align:start position:0%
who's going to which restaurant
under what conditions.

00:30:49.414 --> 00:30:52.350 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm shocked that that
went away at all.

00:30:52.350 --> 00:30:54.719
You think maybe it was
because they were shocked

00:30:54.719 --> 00:30:56.421 align:start size:84% position:16%
in terms of the
population transfers.

00:30:56.421 --> 00:30:57.922
Like the numbers are nuts.

00:30:57.922 --> 00:30:59.858
The amount of people that
have left blue states.

00:30:59.858 --> 00:31:01.326
- And it's also the whole
brain drain thing, right?

00:31:01.326 --> 00:31:02.594
- Yeah.

00:31:02.594 --> 00:31:03.728
- So this was a thing
in Europe and America

00:31:03.728 --> 00:31:05.096
in the '70s and I think '60s

00:31:05.096 --> 00:31:08.933
where you had these
onerous income tax

00:31:08.933 --> 00:31:10.201
from European countries.

00:31:10.201 --> 00:31:11.369
I know this is an
issue in Britain,

00:31:11.369 --> 00:31:12.604 align:start size:84% position:16%
and all the doctors
and engineers,

00:31:12.604 --> 00:31:15.073 align:start size:84% position:16%
and other established
professionals,

00:31:15.073 --> 00:31:16.274
they started fleeing to America.

00:31:16.274 --> 00:31:17.942 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's like, why am I
paying 90% of my income

00:31:17.942 --> 00:31:20.078
when I have a high skilled job,

00:31:20.078 --> 00:31:22.013
I provide for my family
when I could do that

00:31:22.013 --> 00:31:23.548
much better in the states.

00:31:23.548 --> 00:31:25.383
So that is something that
has a historical precedent

00:31:25.383 --> 00:31:26.784
to it as well.

00:31:26.784 --> 00:31:29.687
